``--list-modules`` no longer prints a JSON array of module names. It now prints a table of the modules that can be used with the command it's run with (e.g. ``peat push --list-modules`` only lists modules that can push), honoring ``-d``, ``-I``, and ``-p``, and ``--list-all`` shows a table instead of a list of names. Scripts should use ``--list-modules --json``, which prints a list of objects (use the ``name`` key, e.g. ``jq -r '.[].name'``). Additionally, ``pull`` and ``push`` now skip modules that don't support the command before scanning, and exit with an error if none of the selected modules support it.
